# Intel integrated GPUs that i915 drives without firmware: every generation
# before Skylake (i810 through Broadwell and Cherryview), as listed in the
# kernel's include/drm/i915_pciids.h (v6.10, macros INTEL_I810_IDS to
# INTEL_CHV_IDS). The live initramfs loads i915 at once on these, so the
# panel comes up while the install medium is still being read and the
# console is already a framebuffer at the login (etc/initcpio/hooks/
# omarchy-i915). Skylake and later want DMC, GuC or HuC firmware, 40 MB of it
# across the generations, which stays out of the initramfs: they get i915
# from the live root as before. PCI device IDs, hexadecimal, vendor 8086.
